// NORMAL+ : a bare top-level rule (no #in) runs in the built-in operating states
// INIT and NORMAL, and QUIESCES when the machine enters a special state -- here
// FAILSAFE. `n` counts freely until the guard drives State to FAILSAFE; from the
// next cycle on State==FAILSAFE is outside {INIT,NORMAL}, so the bare `n=n+1`
// stops. The `#in FAILSAFE` block (which DOES run there) latches n into `frozen`,
// proving the bare rule quiesced instead of leaking into the safe state. FAILSAFE
// is sticky, so State never leaves it and n stays put. Runs seq + reactive.
#variable n = 0
#variable frozen = 0

n = n + 1
State = FAILSAFE ? n == 3

#in FAILSAFE
  frozen = n
#end
